skin-mcp — third-party attributions and data provenance
=======================================================

py-monocle / principal graph  (src/skinmcp/vendor/py_monocle/)
--------------------------------------------------------------
The build spec asked for github.com/bioturing/py-monocle to be vendored at a
pinned commit. That repository publishes NO LICENSE — GitHub reports
`NOASSERTION` — so redistributing its source inside this package is not
something we can do.

What ships instead is an independent implementation of the same *published*
algorithm, written from the primary sources:

  * Mao, Wang, Yan & Zeng. "SimplePPT: A Simple Principal Tree Algorithm."
    SIAM International Conference on Data Mining (SDM), 2015.
    — the reverse-graph-embedding objective and its alternating optimisation.
  * Cao, Spielmann, Qiu, ... Trapnell & Shendure. "The single-cell
    transcriptional landscape of mammalian organogenesis." Nature 566, 2019
    (monocle3). — k-means centroid initialisation, MST tree construction,
    spur pruning, and geodesic pseudotime from a root principal point.

It exposes the same `learn_graph` / `order_cells` surface. `skin.traj.monocle`
prefers the real `py_monocle` package when the user has installed it and falls
back to this implementation otherwise; the return field `implementation` records
which one ran, and results are close but not bit-identical.


Mouse–human ortholog table  (src/skinmcp/knowledge/orthologs_mm_hs.tsv)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived from the Mouse Genome Informatics (MGI) vertebrate homology report:
  https://www.informatics.jax.org/downloads/reports/HOM_MouseHumanSequence.rpt
Downloaded 2026-07-31. 24,590 mouse–human symbol pairs; 18,782 are 1:1.
MGI data are freely available for research use; see
http://www.informatics.jax.org/mgihome/other/copyright.shtml
Regenerate with scripts/build_orthologs.py.


Marker sets  (src/skinmcp/knowledge/markers_*.yaml)
----------------------------------------------------
Curated from published skin single-cell work. Primary sources cited inline in
the YAML header; the main ones are:
  Joost et al., Cell Systems 2016 and Cell Stem Cell 2020 (epidermis, HF)
  Philippeos et al., J Invest Dermatol 2018 (dermal fibroblast subsets)
  Buechler et al., Nature 2021 (pan-tissue fibroblast atlas)
  Haensel et al., Cell Reports 2020 (wound)
  Guerrero-Juarez et al., Nat Commun 2019 (wound scRNA-seq)
  Davies, Jenkins, Allen & Taylor, Nat Immunol 2013 (macrophage origin)
  Jaitin et al., Cell 2019; Hill et al., Cell 2018 (LAM/Trem2)
  Ramachandran et al., Nature 2019 (scar-associated macrophages)
  Tirosh et al., Science 2016 (cell-cycle gene sets)
  Reynolds et al., Science 2021 (Human Skin Cell Atlas — referenced for the
  CellTypist Adult_Human_Skin model, not redistributed here)


Enrichment library names  (src/skinmcp/knowledge/enrich_libraries.yaml)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Verified against the live Enrichr catalogue (228 libraries) at
https://maayanlab.cloud/Enrichr/datasetStatistics on 2026-07-31. No Enrichr
gene-set content is redistributed; the file records library *names* and guidance
only. Enrichr: Chen et al., BMC Bioinformatics 2013; Kuleshov et al., NAR 2016.


GO term exclusion preset `skin_irrelevant_v1`
----------------------------------------------
Transcribed from the reference notebook supplied with the build spec
(reference/macrophages_resident_recruited.ipynb, cell 10). It is a
dataset-specific judgement call, ships OFF by default, and every term it drops
is recorded in the tool return and in the figure's sidecar JSON.


R runtime  (src/skinmcp/runtimes/r/)
-------------------------------------
The Dockerfile builds on rocker/r-ver (Rocker Project, GPL-2) and installs
packages from CRAN and Bioconductor per renv.lock. No R package source is
redistributed here; the lockfile pins versions and the image is built locally.
CellChat is installed from github.com/jinworks/CellChat (GPL-3).


